==English==

===Etymology===
From {{NL.}} {{term|glagoliticus|lang=la}}, from {{SH.}} {{term|glagoljica|lang=hr}}/{{term|sc=Cyrl|глагољица|lang=sr}}, from {{OCS.}} {{term|sc=Cyrl|глаголъ|tr=glagolŭ||word, speech|lang=cu}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Of or referring to the [[Glagolitic alphabet]].

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# The oldest known [[Slavonic]] alphabet, created by Saint [[Cyril]] around AD 862–863. It was soon replaced by the [[Cyrillic]] alphabet. The [[Croatian]] variant is still found in use in the Croatian Church along the [[Dalmatia]]n coast. It was the first [[script]] (along with the Croatian language) that was granted special permission by the [[Vatican]] to be used in [[liturgy]] instead of [[Latin]].

